@q 7:44-48

There were **7 years without a Five Year Plan**: 1966-69 (3 years), 1978-80 (2) and 1990-92 (2). The **1990s** were called "**jobless growth**" because output grew fast while jobs grew slowly. The **Twenty Point Programme** (1975) was restructured in 1982, 1986 and 2006.

@section 9.4 | Planned Cities and Yojana

@src 7:49
@pyq U.P.P.C.S. (Pre) 2024
Match List-I with List-II and choose the correct answer using the codes given below the lists:
@match
List-I (Name of the City) | List-II (Period of being Planned)
A. Kanchipuram | 1. Post-independence
B. Jaisalmer | 2. Colonial Period
C. Kodaikanal | 3. Medieval Period
D. Bhilai | 4. Ancient Period
@endmatch
Codes: A B C D
(a) 2 3 4 1
(b) 4 3 2 1
(c) 1 2 3 4
(d) 3 4 1 2
@ans (b)
@end

**Kanchipuram** was a planned Pallava city (ancient); **Jaisalmer** was founded in 1156 (medieval); **Kodaikanal** was a British hill station (1845); **Bhilai** is a steel town built after independence, like Chandigarh and Bhubaneswar.

